	(text_box "POWER MANAGEMENT NOTES:\n- The input power goes through three stages \n  1. a) External Power: LM73100RPWR, 2.7 - 23 V, 5.5 A Integrated Ideal Diode with Input Reverse Polarity and Overvoltage Protection\n     b) USB POWER: SS34-E3/57T Diode\n  2. TPS259531DSGR 2.7V to 18V, 4-A, 34-mΩ eFuse With Fast Overvoltage Protection\n  3. TPS62442RQRR, 2.75-V to 6-V, Dual-Channel Step-Down Converter with Adjustable Frequency\n\n- Stage Description:\n  1. The power is sourced from the imediatelly connected power source without relying on jumpers to manual selection. The diodes prevent current from flowing back to a source in case of multiple ppower sources being conected.\n     The ideal diode was used for thhe external power source to limit power loss inherent in a regular diode as the eternal power source will at times be a battery.   \n     The ideal diode includes ppolarity protection (not required on the USB sources)\n  2. The eFuse provides overvoltage protection, undervoltage lockout, Short Circuit Protection, and limits inrussh current.\n  3. SMPS that outputs two power rails. The first is dedicated and controlled by the ESP32P4 core. The second is general 3.3V power rail used by all other components.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 27.305 29.845 0)
		(size 77.851 55.499)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
