		(uuid "6064f732-fe0b-4c1f-b077-2f11f169ae3e")
	)
	(text_box "ESP32C5 SETUP NOTES:\n1. Set GPIO0 through GPIO MATRIX to GPIO (From 32K XTAL)\n2. Set GPIO1 through GPIO MATRIX to GPI1 (From 32K XTAL)\n3. To enable programming through the JTAG pins eFuse 2: EFUSE_DIS_USB_JTAG has to be set to 1 (default 0)\n   - Set BOOT pins to Joint Download Boot 1 mode (to download through JTAG pins)\n   - In Joint Download Boot 1 mode, the USB Serial/JTAG controller is forcibly disabled, and the JTAG signal only comes from JTAG pins."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 194.564 29.21 0)
		(size 77.216 63.5)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type dash)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7c53a797-9a5a-487d-93ce-3285865f5cd0")
	)
	(text_box "ESP32C5 HARDWARE CONSIDERATIONS:\n- The C5 does not have a USB connector\n  - Programming is to be done through JTAG pins\n  - To enable programming through the JTAG pins eFuse 2: EFUSE_DIS_USB_JTAG has to be set to 1 (default 0)\n- BOOT CONFIGURATION\n  - GPIO26_BOOT is pulled to GND (for all boot configurations) \n  - GPIO27_BOOT and GPIO28_BOOT have PU R with a pull-down BTN\n  - Solder bridge allows for either both to be pulled LOW or only the GPIO28_BOOT"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 27.432 117.602 0)
		(size 77.724 61.722)
		(stroke
